patch_description:
This rewrite uses a fixed equilateral triangular hull of unit area, eliminating the restrictive four-corner square constraint while keeping the normalized objective invariant. The three hull vertices are fixed and the remaining ten points are represented in folded simplex coordinates, guaranteeing that every candidate remains inside the convex region.

The search combines:
- diverse random, stratified, and 3-fold-symmetric initialization;
- vectorized current-to-elite differential evolution;
- lower-tail triangle-area guidance during global exploration;
- a shorter active-constraint polishing phase only for the strongest finalists;
- exact maximin incumbent tracking, with tail area used only as a tie-break.

This removes the expensive polishing of ten candidates for 1,550 iterations each and concentrates final refinement on a small elite set.
